; `uint .size (l..h)` with a NONZERO lower size. RFC 8610 §3.8.1: each admitted size N is a
; maximum (`uint .size N` is `0...256**N`), so the ranged form is the `uint .size h` window and
; generates `u16` here. It once generated `256..65535` (a `2**(8*l)` lower bound that rejected the
; one-byte values). Pinned by `robustness_tests::uint_size_range_lower_bound`.
x = uint .size (1..2)
